{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/VStack","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/HStack","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Spacer","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/RenderCycle"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable"],"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/layoutsystem"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit uses a two-pass layout system inspired by SwiftUI’s layout protocol. Layout containers like "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/VStack","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/HStack","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" first "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"measure","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" each child, then "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"render"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" them with allocated sizes. This approach enables features like flexible spacers, proportional sizing, and proper alignment."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Two Passes","anchor":"The-Two-Passes"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Pass 1: Measure","anchor":"Pass-1-Measure"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The parent proposes a size to each child via ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProposedSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each child responds with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ViewSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that describes how much space it needs and whether it can flex.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["Parent (VStack)","  ├─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Text    → ViewSize(10, 1, flexible: false)","  ├─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Spacer  → ViewSize(0, 0, flexible: true)","  └─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Button  → ViewSize(12, 1, flexible: false)"]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Pass 2: Render","anchor":"Pass-2-Render"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"After measuring all children, the parent distributes the remaining space among flexible children and renders each child with its final allocated size.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["Parent allocates:","  Text   → render(width: 40, height: 1)   \/\/ Gets full width, fixed height","  Spacer → render(width: 40, height: 8)   \/\/ Gets remaining vertical space","  Button → render(width: 40, height: 1)   \/\/ Gets full width, fixed height"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"ProposedSize","anchor":"ProposedSize"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ProposedSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represents the space a parent offers to a child. Either dimension can be ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", meaning “use your ideal size.”","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct ProposedSize {","    public var width: Int?","    public var height: Int?","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Value"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Meaning","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use ideal size (no constraint)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Minimum size"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"> 0"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Available space in characters\/lines"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"text":"ViewSize","level":2,"anchor":"ViewSize","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ViewSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the child’s response: how much space it needs and whether it can expand.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct ViewSize {","    public var width: Int","    public var height: Int","    public var isWidthFlexible: Bool","    public var isHeightFlexible: Bool","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Factory methods make common patterns concise:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["ViewSize.fixed(20, 1)                    \/\/ Fixed 20x1, won't expand","ViewSize.flexible(minWidth: 0, minHeight: 0)  \/\/ Expands in both directions","ViewSize.flexibleWidth(minWidth: 5, height: 1) \/\/ Expands horizontally only"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"The Layoutable Protocol","level":2,"anchor":"The-Layoutable-Protocol","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Views that participate in two-pass layout conform to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Layoutable"},{"text":" (which extends ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Renderable"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["protocol Layoutable: Renderable {","    func sizeThatFits(proposal: ProposedSize, context: RenderContext) -> ViewSize","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A default implementation renders the view and measures the resulting buffer. Custom implementations can calculate size without rendering for better performance.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"ChildView","anchor":"ChildView"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Layout containers wrap their children in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ChildView"},{"type":"text","text":", which provides a uniform interface for measuring and rendering:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct ChildView {","    func measure(proposal: ProposedSize, context: RenderContext) -> ViewSize","    func render(width: Int, height: Int, context: RenderContext) -> FrameBuffer","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ChildView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" automatically detects spacers and propagates child identity for correct state management.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"How Stacks Lay Out Children","anchor":"How-Stacks-Lay-Out-Children"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/VStack"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/HStack"},{"type":"text","text":" follow this algorithm:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Measure","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" all children with the parent’s proposed size"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sum","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the fixed sizes along the stack axis"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Distribute"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" remaining space among flexible children (spacers, flexible text fields, etc.)"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Render","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" each child with its allocated size","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Compose"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" the rendered buffers with the specified spacing and alignment","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Flexible children share remaining space equally. If multiple spacers exist, they each get an equal portion of the leftover space."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Which Views Are Layoutable?","anchor":"Which-Views-Are-Layoutable"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Layoutable?","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Flexibility"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed (wraps at proposed width)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Spacer"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Flexible in stack direction","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Button","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Width-flexible","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/TextField","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"